   "coefficient_ordering": "as exported: column j of X <-> coefficient_names[j], no reordering",
   "conf_int_call": "clubSandwich::conf_int(fit, vcov = <CR2>, test = 'Satterthwaite', level = 0.95)",
   "confidence_level": 0.95,
   "cr2_call": "clubSandwich::vcovCR(fit, cluster = <factor>, type = 'CR2')",
   "intercept_handling": "The design matrix carries its OWN intercept column (all ones) as column 1. The model is fitted with `y ~ 0 + .` so R does NOT add a second intercept. Coefficient order therefore matches the exported coefficient_names exactly.",
   "leverage_adjustment": "CR2 is the bias-reduced linearisation of Bell & McCaffrey / Pustejovsky & Tipton: A_g is the symmetric inverse square root of (I - H_gg) under the identity working model. clubSandwich computes this internally; this script does not supply or override the adjustment matrices.",
   "matrix_tolerance": "clubSandwich's own internal inversion tolerance is used and is NOT overridden here. The Python side clips eigenvalues of (I - H_gg) at 1e-12. These are different mechanisms; any disagreement they cause is a finding, not something to be tuned away.",
   "missing_value_behaviour": "na.action = na.fail. R's default (na.omit) would SILENTLY DROP the row with a missing outcome and return a number, which would be a false agreement. Failing is the correct reference behaviour to compare against.",
   "null_value": 0,
   "satterthwaite_call": "clubSandwich::coef_test(fit, vcov = <CR2>, test = 'Satterthwaite')",
   "target_coefficient": "coefficient_names[target_index_0based + 1] (the slope on x)",
   "working_model_target": "target is left NULL, which for an unweighted lm is the identity working model -- the same homoskedastic-independent working model the Python side assumes. The resolved defaults are recorded in `reference_defaults`."
